-- case_without_branches (or expected_token) at 6:5: the only "branch" is at
-- column 5, equal to the `case` keyword's column, so per §4 it is not inside
-- the case. Whatever follows (`Just` at 7:5) is then a stray token in the
-- body of `f`, so a second syntax error near 7:5 is expected.
f x =
    case x of
    Just n -> n
